### Why did ThreadGroup fail?

ThreadGroup was meant to group threads for bulk control, security boundaries, and uncaught-exception handling. Each aged badly. The bulk-control methods are deprecated. The enumerate methods are racy. The security role was superseded.

```java
// Racy enumerate: count may not match reality
ThreadGroup g = Thread.currentThread().getThreadGroup();
Thread[] arr = new Thread[g.activeCount()];
int count = g.enumerate(arr);  // may miss threads or get stale entries
```

### What does ExecutorService provide that ThreadGroup lacks?

Submit returns a `Future`, shutdown waits for in-flight tasks, and queuing is built in.

```java
ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4);
Future<BigDecimal> nav = pool.submit(() -> calculateNav("SAV2001"));
BigDecimal result = nav.get();  // blocks until result or throws exception
pool.shutdown();
```

### What is StructuredTaskScope?

For related subtasks that form one logical operation, StructuredTaskScope forks them inside a scope and guarantees they all complete or are cancelled together.

```java
try (var scope = new StructuredTaskScope.ShutdownOnFailure()) {
    var balance = scope.fork(() -> getBalance("SAV2001"));
    var trades = scope.fork(() -> getOpenTrades("SAV2001"));
    scope.join().throwIfFailed();
    return new PortfolioView(balance.get(), trades.get());
}
```

### Why does thread naming matter?

A thread dump full of "Thread-0, Thread-1" tells you nothing. A dump full of "settlement-pool-thread-3" tells you which subsystem is stuck.

```java
package com.bank.pool;

import java.util.concurrent.ThreadFactory;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

public class BankThreadFactory implements ThreadFactory {

    private final String prefix;
    private final AtomicInteger counter = new AtomicInteger(0);

    public BankThreadFactory(String prefix) {
        this.prefix = prefix;
    }

    @Override
    public Thread newThread(Runnable r) {
        Thread t = new Thread(r, prefix + "-thread-" + counter.incrementAndGet());
        t.setDaemon(false);
        return t;
    }
}
```

```java
ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4, new BankThreadFactory("settlement-pool"));
// Thread dump now shows: settlement-pool-thread-1, settlement-pool-thread-2, ...
```

### How do the replacements compare?

| Feature | ThreadGroup | ExecutorService | StructuredTaskScope |
|---------|-------------|-----------------|---------------------|
| Return results | No | Yes (Future) | Yes (Subtask) |
| Orderly shutdown | No | Yes | Yes (scope close) |
| Exception propagation | No | Yes (ExecutionException) | Yes (throwIfFailed) |
| Queue management | No | Yes | N/A (scope-based) |
| Bulk cancellation | Deprecated | shutdownNow() | Automatic |

